  "configuration_id": "config_047",
  "reason": "The current best is config_035 (scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) at 0.678 accuracy. The key evidence is that scvi_n200 dramatically outperforms pca_n2000 (+4 pts) and scgpt (+15 pts), and avgpool+weighted is the best aggregation/fusion combo. The remaining uncertainty is whether a stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) complements the richer scvi_n200 representation better than resnet50. With pca_n2000 the image encoder difference was negligible (0.639 vs 0.635), but scvi_n200 produces a more complex learned embedding that may interact differently with a higher-capacity vision backbone. config_047 is a single-variable upgrade of the best config (only image encoder changes), making the result cleanly interpretable. If it improves, it confirms the multimodal synergy hypothesis; if not, it confirms resnet50 is sufficient and we can focus remaining budget on other axes. Expected cost is ~7–8 GPU hours (comparable to config_042 at 7.02 with imagenet_vit_l, slightly above config_035's 5.90 due to the larger ViT-L), which is moderate and well within budget."
}

